N2  - Abstract Nanosatellites are becoming more relevant due to their low-cost ability to complete missions previously reserved for larger satellites. Due to growing interest in this field of technology, the need for attitude determination systems in transmission, Intelligence Survey and Reconnaissance, and other essential satellite reliant industries has become much more prevalent. Attitude determination is a first step towards proper attitude control, which is a gateway to more complex technological advances. A system utilizing a Quaternion Multiplicative Extended Kalman Filter to fuse a multitude of sensors propagated over time, provides accurate attitude determination. Sensors include: two Commercial Off the Shelf gyroscopes, magnetometers, a custom sun sensor, and a small camera that doubles as a star tracker and earth horizon sensor. Furthermore, Accurate position tracking data is obtainable using a Precise Orbit Determination Extended Kalman Filter to ingest raw GPS observables and output filtered position and velocity.
AB  - Abstract Nanosatellites are becoming more relevant due to their low-cost ability to complete missions previously reserved for larger satellites. Due to growing interest in this field of technology, the need for attitude determination systems in transmission, Intelligence Survey and Reconnaissance, and other essential satellite reliant industries has become much more prevalent. Attitude determination is a first step towards proper attitude control, which is a gateway to more complex technological advances. A system utilizing a Quaternion Multiplicative Extended Kalman Filter to fuse a multitude of sensors propagated over time, provides accurate attitude determination. Sensors include: two Commercial Off the Shelf gyroscopes, magnetometers, a custom sun sensor, and a small camera that doubles as a star tracker and earth horizon sensor. Furthermore, Accurate position tracking data is obtainable using a Precise Orbit Determination Extended Kalman Filter to ingest raw GPS observables and output filtered position and velocity.
